  <h2>What I do, in one sentence</h2>
  <p style="font-size:1.1rem">
    <strong>I set up AI systems that run inside your own office, on your own
    computer — so your private information never gets sent over the internet to
    a company like ChatGPT.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Why that matters</h2>
  <p>
    Most AI tools (ChatGPT and the like) work by sending your text, documents,
    or images to a company's servers somewhere else. For a lot of people that's
    fine. But if you're a <strong>law firm, a clinic, an accountant, or any
    business with confidential files</strong>, sending that information to an
    outside company can break your rules — or just feel wrong.
  </p>
  <p>
    I build the same kind of AI — a chatbot, a document searcher, an assistant —
    but it lives <strong>entirely on a computer you own</strong>. Your files
    never leave the building. That's the whole idea. People call it "private AI"
    or "on-premises AI." I call it the obvious choice for anyone handling
    sensitive work.
  </p>

  <h2>What I can build for you</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>A private ChatGPT</strong> for your team — ask it questions, draft documents, summarise files — that never sends a word outside your office.</li>
    <li><strong>A smart search</strong> over your own documents — "find me every contract that mentions X" — running locally.</li>
    <li><strong>Video and image tools</strong> — remove an object from a video, create a narrated video from images, generate a spoken avatar — all on your own machine.</li>
    <li><strong>A health-check service</strong> — once it's set up, I keep it running, backed up, and updated so you don't have to think about it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why me</h2>
  <p>
    I'm honest about how I work: I don't write software by hand in the
    traditional way — I design the system, direct AI tools to build it, and
    then carefully check and operate it. I've spent years in
    <strong>quality control and data security</strong> (the careful,
    rule-following kind of work), which is exactly what you want from someone
    handling your confidential setup. And I prove everything in public — you can
    see my work, including the mistakes I made and fixed, before you ever pay me.
  </p>

  <h2>How to start</h2>
  <p>
    The easiest first step is a <strong>short paid audit</strong>: I look at what
    you have, what you want, and what's possible — and give you a plain written
    report. No commitment beyond that.
  </p>
